docs/entire-core/architecture.md
// Package resourceevents publishes control-plane resource lifecycle
// notifications (org/project/repo and the rest of the coreapi mutations)
// onto NATS so other services — entiredb reaping git data on repo delete,
// entire-search, entire-api — can react. It owns the Event wire format.
//
// Publish delivery is best-effort and at-most-once by design (COR-616): events
// are sent with core NATS (no PubAck wait), so a publish failure is logged and
// swallowed rather than failing the API request that triggered it. PublishAck
// is the explicit acknowledged surface for durable outbox relays; it returns
// every failure and never substitutes for the caller-owned retry anchor. If
// fleet declares a JetStream stream over SubjectPrefix+">" publishes are
// captured durably; absent a stream they are delivered only to live subscribers
// and otherwise dropped.

